<item>
            <title>[LU-20296] Client target recovery/HA mechanism stops choosing a new service node to send SEC_CTX_INIT requests to some OBD device/import</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20296</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;After some servers/VMs have experienced an IB issue, some clients have been found in a state where access to a target can not be restored by recovery/HA mechanism.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This unexpected behaviour is always showing the same set of symptoms like, import stuck in &lt;b&gt;&lt;em&gt;LUSTRE_IMP_CONNECTING&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&#160;state,&#160;&lt;em&gt;&lt;b&gt;SEC_CTX_INIT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&#160;requests timing out and being resent in a loop to a wrong service node/VM without a new alternate&#160;&lt;b&gt;&lt;em&gt;NID&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&#160;being elected, ...&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is interesting to note that both concerned Client/Server versions, respectively&#160;&lt;b&gt;&lt;em&gt;lustre-2.14.0_ddn224&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/b&gt;/&lt;b&gt;&lt;em&gt;lustre-2.14.0_ddn207&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/b&gt;, each contain the full set of patches that have been identified to have &quot;fixed&quot; similar issues before&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A workaround has been found, that is. to manually migrate the concerned target to the expected service node/VM.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And according to Client/Server logs content, associated Lustre versions source code browsing of concerned parts, and forced crash-dump (taken when problem was still alive) analysis, I should able to propose a fix soon since master branch may also be concerned by this problem.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
